    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **60 tests run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved all date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), applying the change consistently across the model, mapper, audit function, and API spec.\n\n**Fiscal-year definition** (`Owner.java`): added a private `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` helper \u2014 a date in July or later belongs to the fiscal year named by its own calendar year; January\u2013June belongs to the fiscal year that began the previous 1 July.\n\n**New `fiscalYear` value** (`Owner.getFiscalYear()`): returns `FY<YY>` derived from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (`YY` = last two digits of the fiscal year), or `null` when no date is set. Exposed as a read-only `fiscalYear` field on `OwnerDto` (added to `openapi.yml`, mapped in `OwnerMapper`).\n\n**Membership identifier's year segment** (`OwnerMapper` + `AuditOwnerCreated`): the `-M<YY>` segment of `membershipNumber` now uses `owner.getFiscalYear().substring(2)` instead of the calendar year, so it always matches the returned `fiscalYear` (verified by Cp14). I updated the audit line too so its independently-built number stays consistent.\n\n**Tenure in elapsed fiscal years** (`Owner.java`): replaced `getTenureDays()` (365-day windows) with `getTenureFiscalYears()` = `fiscalYearOf(today) \u2212 fiscalYearOf(registrationDate)`. The membership-points rule now grants +3 when tenure spans \u2265 1 elapsed fiscal year; a newly created owner still has zero elapsed fiscal years, so the level-4 cap for new owners holds (Cp39/Cp40).\n\nI also updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to match the new fiscal-year semantics.",
